[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]

[size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Elgara Shaders[/b] gives Dragon Age: Origins better materials, shadows and anti-aliasing, through the game's own renderer. Metal reflects, leather and cloth stay matte, shadows are softer and finer. Each feature is an option on the Video tab.[/color][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Whocares66-Dev/DAOElgaraShaders/master/docs/assets/img/cailan.jpg[/img]

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Improved materials[/b]: each material is lit as what it is made of. Metal reflects its surroundings; leather, cloth and stone stay matte. Normal maps shape the light, and highlights roll off instead of clipping.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Armor, weapons and shields from the game, its DLC and Awakening come mapped part by part: a blade is steel, its grip is leather, a shield's rim is iron and its face is wood.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Mods work automatically: their materials are worked out from the game's own item data as you play, and kept.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Improved lighting[/b]: one sun out of doors. Trees, buildings and characters cast soft shadows as the sun falls, and a character in shade is lit as the shade is.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]SMAA[/b] anti-aliasing, [b]exposure[/b] (-0.5 to +0.5), [b]ambient occlusion[/b] (Off to High) and [b]anisotropic filtering[/b] (Off to 16x).[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Every option switches as the game runs. Restore Defaults on the Video tab sets them back. Saves are not modified.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Whocares66-Dev/DAOElgaraShaders/master/docs/assets/img/runic.jpg[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Whocares66-Dev/DAOElgaraShaders/master/docs/assets/img/blooddragon.jpg[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Whocares66-Dev/DAOElgaraShaders/master/docs/assets/img/video-tab.png[/img]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Dragon Age: Origins 1.05. Tested on the GOG version.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dragonage/mods/7052]DAOLib[/url] 0.3.0 or later.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Steam and EA versions: a large-address-aware (LAA) DAOrigins.exe. As installed they run out of memory, with or without this mod.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Extract DAOLib's zip into the game's folder, then this one. To update, extract the new zip over the old files. To uninstall, delete [b]bin_ship\daolib\plugins\elgarashaders[/b].[/color][/size]

[size=4][b]Documentation[/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Read the [url=https://whocares66-dev.github.io/DAOElgaraShaders/]guide[/url]. Source and [url=https://github.com/Whocares66-Dev/DAOElgaraShaders/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md]changelog[/url] are on [url=https://github.com/Whocares66-Dev/DAOElgaraShaders]GitHub[/url], under GPL-3.0. Report problems as a [url=https://github.com/Whocares66-Dev/DAOElgaraShaders/issues]GitHub issue[/url] with [b]elgarashaders.log[/b] from Documents\BioWare\Dragon Age\daolib.[/color][/size]
